// What the fields of entities hold of texts of any length is given back
// when a field gets another text, when its component is removed (in
// place, or by a move to another archetype) or set again, and when its
// entity is destroyed: after thirty rounds of all of that, as many blocks
// are held as fields have bytes. However the program ran.
// RUN: env ENT_TEXT_REPORT=1 %ent run %S/Inputs/text_churn.ent > %t.out 2> %t.err
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HELD --input-file=%t.err
// RUN: env ENT_TEXT_REPORT=1 %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/text_churn.ent 2> %t.perr | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HELD --input-file=%t.perr

// CHECK:      1: 989 notes, 520 extras
// CHECK:      30: 480 notes, 309 extras
// CHECK:      fields with bytes: 675
// HELD:       texts held: 675
